  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the difference and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{8}-3)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{8}\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{9}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1}-3t\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}({1}^{9}-(-1)^{9})-3(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(1+1)-3(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}-6 \\\\  & =-\\frac{52}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
